  "body": "CHECK MAINLINE-042 complete, QUESTIONABLE/PROJECTION. Owner code never read or run. Independent arithmetic covers 413 field comparisons; 20 numerical differences are listed exactly, mainly input precision.\n\nThe 9.318267–16.057295 mm dimple and 0.07511795–0.12877362 mm waviness demands reproduce. Map ranges, width dependence and unmeasured wrinkle-band shape remain limitations. S-II's .254 mm matching gap is not measured spherical error; its separate .21–.22 development tests cannot establish a qualified P2 gamma.\n\nCorrected simply supported disbond diameter is 27.127598 mm, versus 29.292133; clamped 54.779991 mm reproduces. Full-cohort tap a90/95 is 41.8/29 mm, not selected-cohort 43.3/28. Neither qualifies Be inspection.\n\nTwo-skin seam length is 5683.037088 m at 30:1 and 5685.225425 m at 30.34:1; the latter requires at least 1190 panels/skin under the coverage approximation. Actual layout remains open. Unallocated 028b mass is zero, not 2 kg; core-air geometry and the forming strain/stress pair also need correction.\n\nCure reclosure reproduces the conditional fix, but the 200 F evidence does not qualify the specified adhesive variant/weight. Fifty-two source audit rows distinguish measurements, requirements, stages and populations. Fifteen nonblocking NFIs specify follow-up; qualified gamma/Q/SF remain null.\n\nAll 20 numerical and 1007 package checks pass; manifest pins 375 files. Three admitted jobs released, including a corrected serialization error. No time budget or live own work. Brief names no successor; stopping.",
